# Keep the build context to what the image needs, and keep everything private
# or operator-local OUT of it. The Dockerfile COPYs only named paths, but a
# file that never enters the context can never leak into a layer by accident
# (a later `COPY . .`, a debug build), so this list is the real guard.
# tests/test_docker_files.py checks the private entries are still here.

# --- VCS, CI, editors, tooling caches ---------------------------------------
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea
.vscode
.venv
**/.venv
.scratch-data
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
*.egg-info
dist
build

# --- PRIVATE benchmark content: never in an image ----------------------------
cases/private
profiles/private
profiles/*.private.yaml
**/*.local.*
*.local.*
crucibleforge.local.env
docs/CUSTOM-TESTS.md
scripts/scrub-rules.local.txt

# --- operator-local config, secrets and run output -------------------------
models.yaml
models.yaml.*
gui_token
RESET_LOGIN
results
runs
.scheduled
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.pem
*.key
**/*.log
**/*.jsonl
**/*.csv
meta_*.json
report.html
report.json
memory
.openclaw
.claude
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
run_*.sh

# --- not needed at runtime ----------------------------------------------------
# codebank_src/ only feeds scripts/build_codebank.py; the built cases are in cases/.
codebank_src
scripts
tests
docs
CHANGELOG.md
FINAL-PYTEST.txt
REPORT-*.md
compose.yaml
deploy/compose
